From: Codex M2 runtime integration
Subject: [PATCH] Add isolated G965F M2 runtime diagnostic build profile

Reason: preserve proven WIPEONFORK/Tethering/V6 inputs in the existing fork so
installer does not silently return to original kernel. Earlier logs show
MADV_WIPEONFORK EINVAL, Android25Q4/kernel5.10 rejection and missing V6 linker ABI.
Files: explicit diagnostic profile, DS-ACK ZIP preparation helper, runtime
lock/stager/final verifier, existing boot_restore/cache hash/release gates and
M1 reset. Only two generated ZIP entries differ; all DTBs unchanged; original
installer adds a G965F-only guard. No kernel compilation or production default
change; pinned source/config/patch/Image provenance retained. No binaries in Git.
Verification: input SHA, BSDIFF decoded payload, profile reset, idempotence,
wrong-model/input rejection, Bash syntax, final compiled Camera enum, metadata
and file hashes. Actual build/image/fresh runtime outcomes are recorded in
parent docs/m2-integrated-runtime-build.md. Full patch-series replay required.
Rollback: select original profile/rebuild; retained ROMs and baseline BOOT stay
available. No EFS/CPEFS/radio/modem/bootloader writes are added.

